@startuml app_handler_lifecycle_diagram

title GenericTimebaseHandler<T>: One-Shot Lifecycle

hide empty description

state kIdle
state kStarting
state kWorking
state kStopped

kIdle : Handler created, but not started
kStarting : Machine initialization started; result not yet handled
kWorking : Machines are running
kStopped : Handler stopped explicitly or after initialization failure
kStopped : Terminal state; no further processing or restart

[*] --> kIdle
kIdle --> kStarting : Start(token)\n/ start initialization worker
kStarting --> kWorking : RunOnce() [initialization succeeds]\n/ start machines
kIdle --> kStopped : Stop()
kStarting --> kStopped : Stop() or\nRunOnce() [initialization failed]
kWorking --> kStopped : Stop()

@enduml
